                                                "sense_id": "2889bf3c-566e-3188-8150-8a3504816651",
                                                "text": "to take pause",
                                                "translation": "to hesitate",
                                                "english": "to hesitate"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba9f538b-4304-4154-8c48-29423f251ea2",
                                                "sense_id": "2889bf3c-566e-3188-8150-8a3504816651",
                                                "text": "to give pause",
                                                "translation": "to cause to hesitate",
                                                "english": "to cause to hesitate"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69654376-e6b9-45ed-83e3-9bf29d8a1f39",
                                                "sense_id": "2889bf3c-566e-3188-8150-8a3504816651",
                                                "text": "And like a man to double buſsines bound, / I ſtand in pauſe where I ſhall firſt beginne, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b70b40a6-c43e-46b2-af7c-c428d7b7d789",
                                                "sense_id": "2889bf3c-566e-3188-8150-8a3504816651",
                                                "text": "The US House speaker, Mike Johnson, said on Sunday he would have “great pause” about granting a pardon or commutation to Ghislaine Maxwell while another House Republican said it should be considered as part of an effort to obtain more information about Jeffrey Epstein’s crimes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f4e95d10-43c4-3e3e-8efb-ee86b76d45f7",
                                        "entry_id": "3cd4a9fb-9659-3815-8a93-a27eed2b1527",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In writing and printing, a mark indicating the place and nature of an arrest of voice in reading; a punctuation mark."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c955d46-384a-4d38-846e-89b4e25cdec1",
                                                "sense_id": "f4e95d10-43c4-3e3e-8efb-ee86b76d45f7",
                                                "text": "Teach the pupil to mind the pauses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4db975ed-c130-36fa-96c9-4908db0e39a1",
                                        "entry_id": "3cd4a9fb-9659-3815-8a93-a27eed2b1527",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A break or paragraph in writing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b79a3cf3-87a2-4668-a9c6-6df7a3df1185",
                                                "sense_id": "4db975ed-c130-36fa-96c9-4908db0e39a1",
                                                "text": "He [Paul] is full of the Matter he treats and writes with Warmth, which uſually neglects Method, and thoſe Partitions and Pauſes which Men educated in the Schools of Rhetoricians uſually obſerve."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
